# opt-njmpx-nout-last: njmpx=4 and then nout=2 on a later @ line, which one wins (XPPAUT 8.2.2)?
# xpp: rows=5
# pc: ok
# ruling: matches: nout, njmp and a key that starts with njmp set one value, so the last entry wins across @ lines; here nout=2 (crates/pc-ode/docs/language.md, Lists). PhaseCont lists both as njmp in the model info, with the last value.
x'=1
x(0)=0
aux v=x
@ total=4,dt=0.5,meth=euler,njmpx=4
@ nout=2
